  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening National and Local Disaster Preparedness and Response Capacities in Border Areas and Transhumance Corridors in Hodh Ech Chargui Region of Mauritania.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mauritania is extremely vulnerable to the effects of deforestation and drought. As the climate has become warmer, the frequency of wildfires has increased at an alarming rate, posing a serious threat to the dwindling grass and tree cover, destroying pasture and other livelihoods particularly in Hodh Ech Chargui region (HEC). The natural resources degradation and the disappearance of pastures further influences the activities of the population of HEC which are generally breeding livestock. Despite the increasing frequency of disasters, the existing disaster preparedness and operational capacities of the country remain limited. Therefore, the project aims to strengthen the national and local disaster preparedness (DP) and disaster risk reduction (DRR) capacity, through well-informed management with community-based actions, with special focus on the vulnerable communities located in transhumance corridors in HEC. To achieve the objective, IOM will facilitate capacity development of authorities on DP and DRR to implement revised national and HEC regional contingency plans, to strengthen the coordination mechanisms while supporting communities in selected transhumance corridors to enhance local climate resilience and to reinforce local coordination mechanisms in order to anticipate, prevent, and rapidly respond to disasters and resource-related conflict caused by climate change phenomena including unpredictable rains, flooding, drought and wildfires.</narrative>
  </description>
